{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfubYcrudnw8SAnae7WUy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Outcome: RETURN-TO-DRAFT for WI-802.** The verdict and my spec's `## Consolidation` block are committed as `45093b479` with the `WI: WI-900` trailer. The pre-commit hook passed and the worktree is clean. I also ran the kit's own parsers on both: the typed block parses, and the `OUTCOME: RETURN-TO-DRAFT needs=- absorbs=-` line matches it.\n\n**The contradiction.** WI-802 says the review family carries \"WI-847's within-lane retention dial … (shipped off; the merge-gating review is always fresh)\" and that \"WI-847's tests stay green\". That text has not changed since WI-855 on 2026-10-08. On 2026-10-10 the owner ruled (D-008) that the final reviewer is configurable: a fresh session by default, or a persisted independent reviewer. WI-887 builds that and amends SR-227 to match. WI-802 lands after WI-887 through WI-801, WI-800 and WI-858. So a lane built and reviewed against WI-802 as written would take out the persisted mode the owner asked for. It also points at things that don't exist: WI-847 landed with no retention dial and no retention tests; both belong to WI-887. The return note tells the redraft what to fix.\n\n**Nothing absorbed, nothing already done.** WI-875's ruling on the other rows stands, and I didn't revisit it. WI-892 and WI-893 stay separate on purpose: one is a quick move that can land now, the other waits on the owner's ruling of OI-113 (D-015 split them). The bugs behind WI-878 and WI-895 are still present in the code.\n\n**Edges not applied.** Only one outcome can be enacted, so these are in the verdict for you or the next census, which re-runs once WI-802's return changes the queue:\n- WI-801 should wait on WI-878: WI-801 deletes the entry point whose request record WI-878 extends.\n- WI-811 should wait on WI-878: both define how a resolved dispute counts as covered.\n- WI-808 still cites \"WI-828\" for the shared walk, which now belongs to WI-892.\n- OI-113's option (b) is the same thing as WI-808's `Lane-Tip:` trailer. If the owner picks (b), WI-893 should reuse that trailer and wait on WI-808."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":180640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f80396bb-f55f-4bd6-9d86-ff8dd103e989","uuid":"2f1ae5f3-fca8-4616-b99b-aae9c1900dd5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:39:28.022Z","request_id":"req_011CfubYcb2y1EiVFo6Y5158"}
